      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A Rare Opportunity to Acquire a Beautifully Presented Bungalow adjacent to all amenities.\n\nRarely does a detached town bungalow come to the market, making 34 Hollywood Grove, Ballaghaderreen, a particularly appealing opportunity to acquire a superbly located, three-bedroom detached home.\n\nSituated in a quiet and well-established residential area on the edge of town, the property enjoys the best of both worlds — the convenience of town living with the added benefit of open countryside. Overlooking a well-maintained green area to the front and with agricultural lands to the rear, the property offers a pleasant sense of space and a countryside outlook, while remaining within walking distance of all local amenities.\n\nPresented in excellent condition throughout, this attractive bungalow offers bright, comfortable and well-proportioned accommodation, making it an ideal choice for families, retirees, first-time buyers or investors alike.\n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall with tiled flooring, a cosy sitting room featuring a feature fireplace and wood flooring, a fully fitted and tiled kitchen/diner, and a separate utility room. There are three generous double bedrooms, with the master bedroom benefiting from an ensuite, together with a fully tiled family bathroom featuring a separate shower unit.\n\nExternally, the property is complemented by well-maintained grounds, off-street parking and a lovely outlook over the green area, while the agricultural lands to the rear provide an attractive open aspect.\n\nKey Features:\n•Rare opportunity to acquire a detached bungalow in a town setting\n•Superb location on the edge of Ballaghaderreen\n•Open outlook to the rear over agricultural lands\n•Overlooking a well-maintained green area to the front\n•Three spacious double bedrooms, including master ensuite\n•Bright sitting room with feature fireplace\n•Fully fitted kitchen/diner\n•Separate utility room\n•Fully tiled family bathroom with separate shower\n•Oil-fired central heating\n•PVC double-glazed windows\n•Off-street parking\n•Well-maintained grounds\n•Excellent condition throughout\n•Within walking distance of all town amenities\n\nLocation:\nIdeally positioned on the edge of Ballaghaderreen, the property is within walking distance of National and Secondary Schools, playgrounds, sporting facilities, shops, pubs, restaurants and the Cathedral.\n\nIreland West Airport is less than a 20-minute drive away. Regular bus services operate from the town to Dublin and Ballina, with Local Link bus services connecting to Sligo.\n\nThis beautifully maintained bungalow offers a wonderful combination of town convenience, a peaceful residential setting and an open countryside aspect. Whether you are seeking a family home, a place to retire or an investment property, 34 Hollywood Grove is an opportunity not to be missed.\n\nViewing of this beautiful home is highly recommended and by appointment only\n\n"
      },
